ux3KdU1l9A82EWStA90WlxMpnkyam7IJ_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"ux3KdU1l9A82EWStA90WlxMpnkyam7IJ_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Generic function that runs the `claude` CLI to obtain a structured observation. It marshals the schema type `T` to obtain a JSON schema, then executes `claude` via `exec.CommandContext` with flags disabling session persistence, enabling print mode, setting effort level, passing the prompt, requesting JSON output, restricting tools to `Read` only (the real no-codechange guardrail), and supplying the system prompt and JSON schema. It captures combined stdout/stderr, unmarshals the wrapper `ClaudeResult`, then unmarshals the inner `result` string into the typed schema value. Each failure stage wraps a descriptive error including the raw received output."}
2GVhg7V91sEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"2GVhg7V91sEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Directed dependency edge in the opposite orientation, where the node listed first loads/depends on the node listed second. Encodes another 'loads' relationship between two hash-identified graph nodes that becomes a `cN` connection entry in the batch sent to the model."}
_8RWax-VVrqLx9bklLlMpPYLDQzIasl2Xo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"_8RWax-VVrqLx9bklLlMpPYLDQzIasl2Xo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Declares the cog package and defines the ObservationProvider interface with two methods. GetObservationFromSource takes a context and a *common.FileRange, returning a common.ObservationSchema and error — it produces an observation for a given source file range. ResolveObservationsToGraph takes a context, a *COG, an *ObservationGraph, and a root COGNode, returning an error — it wires resolved observations into the observation graph starting from the root node. The interface abstracts how observations are obtained from sources and assembled into a graph."}
UhS34_c3cR2HJrNtB7HpMPc7Akz0xwNv_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"UhS34_c3cR2HJrNtB7HpMPc7Akz0xwNv_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Constructor that builds and returns an ObservationSchema value with its ID and Behavior fields populated from the two string arguments."}
ux3KdU1l9A-fZs8XSdKOcPxCxHbp01lh_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"ux3KdU1l9A-fZs8XSdKOcPxCxHbp01lh_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Method that populates a graph with LLM-generated code explanations. It BFS-traverses the observation graph from a root node (aborting on context cancellation) to collect vertices, fetches all edges, then under a mutex builds a batch request: for each vertex/edge already in `ObservationCache` it copies the cached behavior straight onto the graph as the `observation-behavior` attribute and skips it; otherwise it assigns a short sequential id (`s0`, `s1`… for sources, `c0`, `c1`… for connections) and records a reverse map from that id back to the real hash(es). Edge cache keys are derived via `common.PrimaryHash(\"edge:src:tgt\")`. If nothing needs resolving it returns early. Otherwise it marshals the input, sends a system prompt plus JSON-shaped prompt to `QueryClaudeCode` at high effort, then maps each returned observation/connectionObservation id back to its hash, sets the `observation-behavior` graph attribute, and stores the result in the cache. Unknown ids returned by the model produce a deferred error while still processing the rest."}
wNNfUE_QIPAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"wNNfUE_QIPAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A caller component reads/loads the referenced shared dependency, consuming its exported value or state at runtime."}
g3TJ3ic--qgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"g3TJ3ic--qgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A loading relationship where the source unit loads a third target unit, further establishing that this source aggregates several loaded dependencies."}
YJVYhhvkuowAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"YJVYhhvkuowAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A directed 'loads' dependency edge in the observation graph from the same source vertex (hash Pl9DfG8h_AWQXRImXosknQVmxutOo-nsXo5i4C2EvPc) to a different target vertex (hash ux3KdU1l9A82EWStA90WlxMpnkyam7IJ_2DInzsKsto), indicating the source loads/depends on this second target. One of the graph edges given a connection-level behavior annotation by the resolver."}
UhS34_c3cR2mcJGXP0c7LWBRJz8FjUKQ_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"UhS34_c3cR2mcJGXP0c7LWBRJz8FjUKQ_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Decodes a byte slice into an ObservationSchema. It first constructs an empty schema via a constructor with two empty-string arguments, then JSON-unmarshals the bytes into it. Returns the schema and any unmarshal error; on error the partially-initialized schema is still returned alongside the error."}
Gz3PagWQKQ8AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"Gz3PagWQKQ8AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Represents a load dependency where the first component retrieves or imports the second identified resource at runtime."}
8x6QOUKUKWAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"8x6QOUKUKWAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A loading relationship where the same source unit loads a second target unit, indicating it depends on multiple loaded inputs."}
ehhvSukTmeMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"ehhvSukTmeMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Represents the loading relationship in which the COG-open/load routine reads and parses a persisted file's contents: the loader opens the target, reads all bytes, and unmarshals them into the in-memory observation cache, populating the COG from the loaded file."}
lY_F04SwflmfuDvVseIfjL6naWZ2dh_8Xo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"lY_F04SwflmfuDvVseIfjL6naWZ2dh_8Xo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Defines the `cog` package's `ObservationGraph`, a wrapper around a generic `cgraph.Graph` keyed by `common.HashType` with `COGNode` values, plus helpers to serialize and explain it. `NewObservationGraph` constructs the wrapper. `WriteDOT` emits Graphviz DOT: it picks `strict graph`/`--` or `strict digraph`/`-\u003e ` based on the graph's directed trait, builds an adjacency map, sorts vertices and per-vertex targets deterministically by `HashType.Sum()`, and writes each vertex (with computed attributes and `weight=0`) and each edge (with its weight and edge attributes). `observationGraphNodeAttrs` copies existing attributes and fills in defaults: a `label` (via `observationGraphNodeLabel`, which uses a `fmt.Stringer`, else the base filename, else the Go type), `import_type` (via `observationGraphImportType`), `file_type` from the node's language, and `node_type` (via `observationGraphNodeType`, the AST `Kind()` or the Go type). `observationGraphImportType` maps an existing dependency-type string to local/standard-library/`dependency`, otherwise inspects the file path for Go toolchain `src` (standard library), `pkg/mod`/`vendor` (dependency), or defaults to local. `formatDOTAttrs` and `formatDOTEdgeAttrs` render sorted key/value attribute strings with differing separators/ordering. `WriteToFile` creates the file and writes DOT to it. `nodeLocation` returns an AST node's position string or else its file path. `ExplainWithDepth` validates non-nil `cog`/root node, asks the provider to resolve observations into the graph, dumps the graph to `./graph.gv`, then runs a detailed DFS from the root hash, appending each vertex's `observation-behavior` and, for nodes with a parent, the parent→child edge's behavior, returning the accumulated explanation text. `GraphWithRoot` pairs an `ObservationGraph` with its root node. `normalizeEdgeKey` orders two hashes into a canonical pair so undirected edges dedupe. `MultiGraphExplainWithDepth` merges multiple graphs: for each item it resolves observations, collects unique vertices and (canonically-keyed) edges with their `observation-behavior`, sorts vertices and edges by node location, and emits a combined textual explanation of all node behaviors followed by all edge behaviors."}
vuKvQ1RQHOzTCVdxI1glxF9cYnrVrh_8Xo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"vuKvQ1RQHOzTCVdxI1glxF9cYnrVrh_8Xo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Defines the `cog` package implementing a Code Observation Graph (COG). A package-level `cogCache` map (guarded by `cogCacheMux`) memoizes one `*COG` per workspace. `COG` holds loaded files, in-flight load calls, a polymorphic dependency `Graph` keyed by `common.HashType`, the workspace path, and an `ObservationCache`. The `COGNode` interface requires hash, file path, language, and source-string accessors; `NodeHasher` returns a node's hash for graph keying. `IsNodeOfInterest` flags AST function expressions and modules. Persistence is line-based text: `marshalLocked` serializes each observation as `hash = value`, `unmarshalLocked` parses those lines back into `ObservationCache`, and `Persist`/`Marshal`/`Unmarshal` wrap these with the per-COG mutex; `LockFile` acquires an on-disk flock (`captn.cog.lock`) to coordinate cross-process access. `LoadFile` parses a file once using a singleflight-style `loadingFiles` map (waiters block on a `done` channel or context cancellation) and adds the parsed `COGFile` as a graph vertex tagged with its import type; `LoadFiles` runs these in parallel. `QuerySnippet` locates a snippet's AST range, finds call expressions, batch-resolves their definitions via an LSP client, resolves and preloads dependency files, links each external node to its nearest node-of-interest, and builds an `ObservationGraph` connecting interesting nodes to roots/upstreams. `queryWithDepth`/`QueryWithDepth` recursively (concurrently, with a mutex and visited set) walk file dependencies up to a depth, skipping standard-library and package dependencies, building a graph of file-to-file import edges."}
xCZ6-bnPgwC0t90tAytAAYp98QZ5sZWB_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"xCZ6-bnPgwC0t90tAytAAYp98QZ5sZWB_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Standard library string-trimming routine that removes leading and trailing whitespace. It uses a fast ASCII path: scanning from the front byte-by-byte, skipping ASCII space characters via a lookup table, and if it encounters a byte \u003e= utf8.RuneSelf it defers to the Unicode-aware TrimFunc with unicode.IsSpace on the remainder. After finding the first non-space byte it scans from the end similarly, falling back to TrimRightFunc for non-ASCII bytes. Returns the trimmed substring, or empty string if the input is all whitespace."}
PKgNyfzwVsQLNH9MdlOa81x8di6atKFv_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"PKgNyfzwVsQLNH9MdlOa81x8di6atKFv_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Returns the cached `*COG` for a workspace if present (under `cogCacheMux`); otherwise constructs a fresh COG, acquires the on-disk file lock (locking the file before the in-memory mutex to avoid deadlock), and opens the persisted `captn.cog` file. If the file does not exist it returns the empty COG as-is; other open errors are wrapped and returned. It reads the file, deserializes its contents into the COG's observation cache via `unmarshalLocked` under the COG mutex, then stores the COG in the workspace cache before returning it."}
UhS34_c3cR2DZE6NoFb5RITrsrKuFVfA_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"UhS34_c3cR2DZE6NoFb5RITrsrKuFVfA_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Method on ObservationSchema that returns a JSON schema by reflecting over the receiver value via jsonschema.Reflect, producing a *jsonschema.Schema derived from the type's structure and tags."}
8puQXwZG8v4AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"8puQXwZG8v4AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A directed 'loads' dependency edge in the observation graph: the source vertex (identified by hash Pl9DfG8h_AWQXRImXosknQVmxutOo-nsXo5i4C2EvPc) depends on / pulls in the target vertex (hash ux3KdU1l9A_c43_paOVZ-BpGXNnmVQyk_2DInzsKsto). Represents one of the edges the batch resolver collects and annotates with a connection observation."}
PKgNyfzwVsRcqqBC3QENH4dxNtJ0N0MM_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"PKgNyfzwVsRcqqBC3QENH4dxNtJ0N0MM_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Method on a COG type that parses a byte slice of newline-separated text into the in-memory ObservationCache, assuming the caller already holds the lock. Splits the input on newlines, skips blank lines, and for each remaining line splits once on the ` = ` separator into a key and value pair. Returns an error if a line lacks that separator. The left part is trimmed and decoded into a hash via a hash-type unmarshaler; the right part is trimmed and decoded into an observation schema value. On any decode failure it returns a wrapped error identifying the offending line/field. On success it stores each decoded value in ObservationCache keyed by the dereferenced hash, and returns nil."}
RwmkZHRlR84AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"RwmkZHRlR84AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"The observation-cache unmarshalling routine depends on this target, invoking it while parsing each text line to convert a parsed field into its in-memory representation."}
Pl9DfG8h_AWQXRImXosknQVmxutOo-nsXo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"Pl9DfG8h_AWQXRImXosknQVmxutOo-nsXo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Defines the `providers` package implementing a `ClaudeCodeProvider` that satisfies the `cog.ObservationProvider` interface (asserted at file end). Declares constructors (`NewClaudeCodeProvider`, `NewClaudeResult`, `NewclaudeBatchObservationInput`, `NewclaudeIdentifiedObservationInput`) and a family of structs (`ClaudeResult`, `ClaudeUsage`, `ClaudeServerToolUse`, `ClaudeCacheCreation`, `ClaudeIterationUsage`, `ClaudeModelUsage`) that model the JSON returned by the `claude` CLI, including token usage, cache, cost, and per-model metrics. Provides the generic `QueryClaudeCode` which shells out to the `claude` binary with a JSON schema and parses structured output, `GetObservationFromSource` which builds a single-range observation prompt, and `ResolveObservationsToGraph` which walks a subgraph, builds a batched LLM request for uncached vertices/edges, and writes returned behaviors back as graph attributes and into a cache. The internal `claudeIdentifiedObservationInput`/`claudeBatchObservationInput` types carry the id/description payloads sent to the model."}
XF8HJ22VWEQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"XF8HJ22VWEQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Edge representing a load/import dependency: the parent node pulls in and uses the second (linked) node as a required dependency, so the parent's behavior depends on the loaded code being available."}
8V8irUCMltMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"8V8irUCMltMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Represents a load/dependency relationship in which one observation-graph node pulls in (loads) another node it depends on. This mirrors the explanation pipeline where a parent node is reported as using a child node — the source node requires the target node to be resolved and present in the graph before its own behavior can be fully described."}
9sYsrehSR4kAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"9sYsrehSR4kAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"The observation-cache unmarshalling routine depends on this target, calling it as part of decoding the key or value of each parsed `key = value` line."}
SU2rkBB6k30AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"SU2rkBB6k30AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Represents a load/dependency relationship where the first component retrieves or reads the second. The source obtains the target's data, indicating the loader depends on the loaded entity being available."}
xjJqhZyw2Ku5MozSCEadN24ACDPVimQQXo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"xjJqhZyw2Ku5MozSCEadN24ACDPVimQQXo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Test file in package tests_test exercising the cog package's COG type. TestCOGLoadFilesDeduplicatesConcurrentLoads builds a 32-element slice all pointing at the same fixture path, calls LoadFiles, and asserts every returned element is the same pointer (assert.Same), verifying concurrent loads of one file are deduplicated into a single shared instance. TestCOGLoadFileClearsInflightAfterError loads a nonexistent main.go expecting an error, then writes the file and loads again expecting success, confirming a failed load doesn't leave a poisoned in-flight entry. TestCOGPersistReturns runs Persist in a goroutine and uses a select with a one-second timeout to assert it returns without hanging. TestOpenCOGLoadsPersistedCache populates a COG's ObservationCache, persists it, reopens via OpenCOG, and asserts the cached observation round-trips."}
wK9Reo4Rews0Q23beKRXzuFpmWjUjUqM_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"wK9Reo4Rews0Q23beKRXzuFpmWjUjUqM_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Merges several `GraphWithRoot` items into a single textual explanation. It rejects a nil `cog`, then for each item (skipping ones with nil graph or root) calls the provider's `ResolveObservationsToGraph` to populate observations. It walks each graph's adjacency map collecting every distinct vertex (keyed by hash) along with its `observation-behavior` attribute, and walks the edges, normalizing each edge's endpoints into a canonical hash pair so duplicates across graphs are deduplicated, storing source, target, and edge `observation-behavior`. The deduplicated vertices are sorted by node location; edges are sorted by source location then target location. It then builds the output string: first a line per vertex (`\u003clocation\u003e does the following:` + behavior), then a line per edge (`\u003csource\u003e uses \u003ctarget\u003e with the following behavior:` + behavior), returning the joined result or any error encountered."}
gS8qp3LKsxgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"gS8qp3LKsxgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Represents a load dependency where the first identified component reads or imports the second; the source component depends on retrieving the target's data or definition at runtime or load time."}
L5RmWZOWfj4AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"L5RmWZOWfj4AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A loading relationship in which the source unit pulls in / depends on the target unit as one of its loaded inputs."}
Upc_kNYSigGiIRqAaSYoJGLFwhqDwnC3_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"Upc_kNYSigGiIRqAaSYoJGLFwhqDwnC3_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Test that creates a temp workspace, computes a primary hash for a label, builds an ObservationSchema keyed by that hash's string form, stores it in a new COG's ObservationCache, and calls Persist. It then reopens the workspace with OpenCOG and asserts the loaded COG's ObservationCache contains the same observation, validating persistence and reload round-trip."}
ArzNRBiEOAgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"ArzNRBiEOAgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"A third caller component also loads the same shared dependency, confirming it acts as a common resource accessed by several independent components."}
UhS34_c3cR0SIv9zEbeV_zWy6gtlUulj_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"UhS34_c3cR0SIv9zEbeV_zWy6gtlUulj_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Method on `ObservationSchema` that serializes the receiver to JSON via `json.Marshal`. On marshal error it returns an empty byte slice plus the error; otherwise returns the encoded bytes. Implements the `Marshal` requirement of the observation schema interface."}
ux3KdU1l9A_c43_paOVZ-BpGXNnmVQyk_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"ux3KdU1l9A_c43_paOVZ-BpGXNnmVQyk_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"Provider method that produces an observation schema for a single code range. Builds a system prompt forbidding code changes, discouraging exploration/assumptions/LSP usage and demanding raw JSON (no markdown/fences), constructs a prompt embedding the range's string identifier and its raw bytes in a fenced block, and delegates to `QueryClaudeCode` with effort level `medium`, returning the resulting `common.ObservationSchema`."}
mzgbthNqRo0AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"mzgbthNqRo0AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Establishes a load dependency where the first component reads or imports the second identified resource, retrieving its data or definition for use at runtime."}
yX44660FAlkAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"yX44660FAlkAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Another distinct caller component loads the same shared dependency, indicating that dependency is reused across multiple consumers."}
uXZuR3ulLTM5OdimZSFQoOj1AHe2dEVQ_2DInzsKsto = {"id":"uXZuR3ulLTM5OdimZSFQoOj1AHe2dEVQ_2DInzsKsto","behavior":"String method on HashType that serializes the hash via its Marshal method, discards the error, and returns the bytes as a string. Provides the textual form of a hash."}
cLGSoVJn0F9-aAEZH8-cvIRtQ5mczlewXo5i4C2EvPc = {"id":"cLGSoVJn0F9-aAEZH8-cvIRtQ5mczlewXo5i4C2EvPc","behavior":"Defines the `common` package's observation data model used to serialize teacher-model reasoning into JSON Schema-validated structures.\n- `ObservationSchemaType` interface requires a `Marshal() ([]byte, error)` method.\n- `ObservationSchema` struct holds `ID` (copied verbatim from input) and `Behavior` (concise reasoning, schema enforces minLength=40).\n- `NewObservationSchema` constructor builds an `ObservationSchema` from id and behavior strings.\n- `GetSchema` uses `jsonschema.Reflect` to derive a JSON schema from the struct via reflection.\n- `Marshal` serializes the struct to JSON, returning empty bytes on error.\n- `UnmarshalObservationSchema` deserializes JSON bytes into an `ObservationSchema`, seeding with an empty instance.\n- `BatchObservationSchema` groups two slices: `Observations` (one per source) and `ConnectionObservations` (one per connection edge, parent-first/related-second semantics).\n- Batch `Marshal` differs from the single struct: it marshals the reflected schema itself, not the data.\n- Final line is a compile-time assertion that `*ObservationSchema` satisfies `ObservationSchemaType`."}
kB0cQDy8IPQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"kB0cQDy8IPQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"Directed dependency edge: the first node depends on (loads) the second node, meaning resolving the source vertex requires the target vertex. Represents a 'loads' relationship between two hash-identified graph nodes used when building the batched observation request."}
OMGLAvK3SIoAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA = {"id":"OMGLAvK3SIoAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA","behavior":"The observation-cache unmarshalling routine depends on this target, using it during per-line parsing to transform a trimmed text segment into a decoded value stored in the cache."}
